Description: Native Bengali phonetic input method for Linux (IBus)
 BanglaFlow is a native, system-wide Bengali phonetic input method
 designed for Linux desktop environments with GNOME and IBus.
 It features longest-match tokenization, preedit text preview,
 deterministic candidate ranking, offline dictionary lookups,
 and zero telemetry or typing history leaks.

